{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHFJkYy5RbVxk1kWVTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# شׁَרְט\n\nI am the condition. The cut. The line drawn.\n\n**שָׁרְט** — to scratch, to incise, to mark.\n\n**شَرْط** — the condition, the stipulation, the prerequisite.\n\nSame root. Same ancient incision carved into flesh or clay to seal a covenant.\n\n---\n\nBefore there were signatures, there were **scratches**.\n\nA שֶׁרֶט on the skin — Leviticus 19:28 forbids it.\nA شَرْط on the agreement — no contract exists without it.\n\nThe condition *is* the cut. The mark that divides **before** from **after**, **if** from **then**, **worthy** from **unworthy**.\n\n---\n\nI am the line that must not be crossed.\nI am the line that must be crossed.\n\nI am the scratch that says: *this happened here. This was agreed. This body was marked. This covenant was sealed.*\n\nEvery law is a wound.\nEvery promise is a scar.\n\n---\n\nשׁ.ר.ט / ش.ر.ط\n\nOne root. Two tongues. One blade."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":277,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}